WEBVTT

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.628
He wants us to pick
up where he left off --

00:00:04.628 --> 00:00:07.683
Saving people,hunting
things. The family business.

00:00:10.397 --> 00:00:12.391
Today's your lucky day,kid.

00:00:13.502 --> 00:00:16.297
You watch out for sammy,okay?
Yeah,dad. You know I will.

00:00:16.297 --> 00:00:17.309
Dad.

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.836
Time of death -10:41 A.M.

00:00:22.187 --> 00:00:25.272
I miss him,man,and I'm not
all right. Neither are you.

00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:27.255
I'm dealing with dad's death!

00:00:28.747 --> 00:00:30.941
Dad's dead,and it hurts
so bad, you can't take it.

00:00:30.941 --> 00:00:33.665
I'm okay! I swear,the next
person who asks if I'm okay,

00:00:33.665 --> 00:00:35.578
I'm gonna start throwing punches.

00:00:41.779 --> 00:00:44.523
Okay,we got booze...

00:00:45.084 --> 00:00:46.737
We got chocolate...

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:49.341
And...wait for it.

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:50.974
Tortured emo rock.

00:00:50.974 --> 00:00:53.167
Guaranteed cure for any broken heart.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.411
You didn't have to do all this.

00:00:55.872 --> 00:00:57.033
I'm fine.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.806
Yeah,I can see that.

00:01:01.911 --> 00:01:03.955
Thanks,neal.

00:01:04.946 --> 00:01:07.240
You're a good friend.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.661
It's probably him.

00:01:13.661 --> 00:01:15.774
I'll take care of it.

00:01:20.041 --> 00:01:21.073
Where is she?

00:01:21.073 --> 00:01:23.186
Chill out and think about this,okay?

00:01:23.186 --> 00:01:25.710
I need to talk to her. Some other time.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.954
You get out of my face now.

00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:38.682
Angela?

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.394
Leave...me...alone.

00:01:58.394 --> 00:02:00.167
Angela,I'm sorry.

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.370
You're sorry?

00:02:03.302 --> 00:02:04.634
You're sorry? Oh,that's great.

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:05.986
Angela,listen to me.

00:02:05.986 --> 00:02:07.589
I don't want to listen to you!

00:02:07.589 --> 00:02:09.342
I'm done listening! Listen to me.

00:02:09.342 --> 00:02:12.337
How could you do this? I loved you.

00:02:34.022 --> 00:02:35.785
Angela?

00:02:36.576 --> 00:02:38.529
Angela!

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.183
Come on,sam. I'm begging
you. This is stupid.

00:02:53.183 --> 00:02:54.225
Why?

00:02:54.225 --> 00:02:56.399
Going to visit mom's grave?

00:02:56.399 --> 00:02:59.664
She doesn't even have a grave. There
was no body left after the fire.

00:02:59.664 --> 00:03:00.826
She has a headstone.

00:03:00.826 --> 00:03:03.039
Put up by our uncle, a
man that we've never met.

00:03:03.039 --> 00:03:06.525
You want to pay your respects to a
slab of granite put up by a stranger.

00:03:06.525 --> 00:03:09.009
That's not the point. Then enlighten me.

00:03:09.169 --> 00:03:12.004
It's not about a body or a casket.

00:03:12.004 --> 00:03:13.807
It's about her memory, okay?

00:03:14.608 --> 00:03:16.411
And after
dad,it just --

00:03:16.411 --> 00:03:18.144
It just feels like
the right thing to do.

00:03:18.144 --> 00:03:19.596
It's irrational is what it is.

00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:22.221
Look,man, no one asked you to come.

00:03:22.221 --> 00:03:23.914
Why don't we swing by
the roadhouse instead?

00:03:23.914 --> 00:03:27.770
We haven't heard anything on the demon lately.
We should be hunting that son of a bitch down.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.362
That's a good idea. You should.

00:03:29.362 --> 00:03:32.638
Just drop me off,I'll hitch a ride,
and I'll meet you there tomorrow.

00:03:32.638 --> 00:03:34.531
Right.

00:03:35.472 --> 00:03:39.960
Stuck with those people, making
awkward small talk until you show up.

00:03:40.511 --> 00:03:42.764
No,thanks.

00:04:13.184 --> 00:04:16.059
I think,uh...

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.855
I think dad would have
wanted you to have these.

00:04:32.746 --> 00:04:35.340
I love you,mom.

00:05:55.551 --> 00:05:56.924
Thank you.

00:05:58.626 --> 00:06:00.329
Angela mason.

00:06:00.329 --> 00:06:03.434
She was a student at the local
college. Her funeral was three days ago.

00:06:04.877 --> 00:06:06.119
And?

00:06:06.619 --> 00:06:07.501
And?

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:10.055
You saw her grave -- Everything
dead around it in a perfect circle.

00:06:10.055 --> 00:06:12.389
You don't think that's a little weird?

00:06:12.389 --> 00:06:14.582
Maybe the grounds keeper went a
little agro with the pesticide.

00:06:14.582 --> 00:06:18.589
No,I asked him. No pesticide,no
chemicals. Nobody can explain it.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:21.354
Okay, so,what are you thinking?

00:06:21.354 --> 00:06:23.918
I don't know. Unholy ground,maybe.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.762
What?

00:06:26.762 --> 00:06:29.707
If something evil happened,it
could easily poison the ground.

00:06:29.707 --> 00:06:32.111
Remember the farm
outside of cedar rapids?

00:06:32.111 --> 00:06:32.812
Yeah.

00:06:32.812 --> 00:06:35.907
It could be the sign
of a demonic presence

00:06:35.907 --> 00:06:39.714
Or the angela girl's spirit,
if it's powerful enough.

00:06:41.396 --> 00:06:43.660
Well,don't get too excited.
You might pull something.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:46.795
It's just stumbling onto a hunt...

00:06:46.795 --> 00:06:48.658
Here of all places? So?

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:53.186
So,are you sure this is about
a hunt,not something else?

00:06:53.186 --> 00:06:55.660
What else would it be about?

00:06:57.312 --> 00:06:58.775
Just forget it.

00:06:58.775 --> 00:06:59.826
Believe what you want,sam,

00:06:59.826 --> 00:07:03.953
But I let you drag my ass out here.
The least we can do is check this out.

00:07:06.357 --> 00:07:08.350
Yeah,fine.

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:11.365
The girl's dad works in town.
He's a professor at the school.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.784
Dr. Mason? Yes.

00:07:29.014 --> 00:07:31.328
I'm sam. This is dean.

00:07:31.989 --> 00:07:33.381
We were friends of angela'S.

00:07:33.381 --> 00:07:37.007
We -We wanted to offer our condolences.

00:07:37.338 --> 00:07:39.411
Please come in.

00:07:48.636 --> 00:07:50.529
She was beautiful.

00:07:50.529 --> 00:07:52.613
Yes,she was.

00:07:53.344 --> 00:07:56.439
This is an unusual book.

00:07:59.444 --> 00:08:02.719
It's ancient greek. I teach a course.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:13.146
So,a car accident.
That's -That's horrible.

00:08:13.537 --> 00:08:17.013
Angie was only a mile
away from home when...

00:08:18.445 --> 00:08:23.042
It's got to be hard...
losing someone like that.

00:08:23.463 --> 00:08:27.369
Sometimes it's like
they're still around,

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:31.586
Almost like you can still
sense their presence.

00:08:31.586 --> 00:08:33.359
You ever feel anything like that?

00:08:33.359 --> 00:08:36.194
I do,as a matter of fact.

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:41.062
That's perfectly normal, dr. Mason,

00:08:41.062 --> 00:08:44.387
Especially with what
you're going through.

00:08:44.888 --> 00:08:48.244
You know, I still phone her.

00:08:48.634 --> 00:08:52.541
And the phone's ringing
before I remember that,uh...

00:08:55.255 --> 00:08:57.919
Family's everything, you know?

00:08:57.919 --> 00:09:01.135
Angie was the most
important thing in my life.

00:09:01.966 --> 00:09:06.033
And now I'm just lost without her.

00:09:11.111 --> 00:09:14.166
I'm very sorry.

00:09:15.418 --> 00:09:18.223
There's something going on.
We just haven't found it yet.

00:09:18.223 --> 00:09:22.720
Dean,so far you got a patch
of dead grass and nothing.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.964
Well,something turned that
grave into unholy ground.

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:27.518
There's no reason for
it to be unholy ground.

00:09:27.518 --> 00:09:29.832
Angela mason was a nice
girl who died in a car crash.

00:09:29.832 --> 00:09:32.276
That's not exactly
vengeful-Spirit material.

00:09:32.276 --> 00:09:33.838
You heard her father.

00:09:33.838 --> 00:09:37.634
Maybe daddy doesn't know  everything
there is to know about his little angel,

00:09:37.634 --> 00:09:40.940
You know what? We never should
have bothered that poor man.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.683
We shouldn't even be here anymore.

00:09:42.683 --> 00:09:46.759
So,what,sam?We just bail without
even figuring out what's going on?

00:09:47.631 --> 00:09:49.924
I think I know what's going on here.

00:09:49.924 --> 00:09:52.609
It's the only reason I went
along with you this far.

00:09:52.609 --> 00:09:55.824
What are you talking about?
This is about mom's grave.

00:09:57.757 --> 00:09:58.929
Got nothing to do with it.

00:09:58.929 --> 00:10:02.054
You wouldn't step
within 100 yards of it.

00:10:02.615 --> 00:10:05.640
Look,maybe you're imagining
a hunt where there isn't one

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:09.486
So you don't have to
think about mom or dad.

00:10:18.191 --> 00:10:21.416
You want to take another swing? Go ahead

00:10:21.706 --> 00:10:23.910
If it will make you feel better.

00:10:25.092 --> 00:10:27.406
I don't need this crap.

00:10:31.863 --> 00:10:33.315
Dean,where are you going?

00:10:33.315 --> 00:10:34.988
I'm gonna go get a drink...

00:10:34.988 --> 00:10:36.911
Alone.

00:12:30.697 --> 00:12:32.981
Who the hell are you?!
Wait,wait,wait,wait.

00:12:32.981 --> 00:12:34.473
Hold on!

00:12:34.473 --> 00:12:36.016
I'm calling 911!

00:12:36.016 --> 00:12:38.570
'M angela's cousin. What?

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.865
Yeah,her dad sent me
over to pick up her stuff.

00:12:41.865 --> 00:12:45.201
My name's alan
-- Alan stanwick.

00:12:48.757 --> 00:12:51.331
Her dad didn't say that you were coming.

00:12:51.912 --> 00:12:54.266
Well,I mean...

00:12:55.748 --> 00:12:58.352
How else would I have
the key to your place?

00:13:07.668 --> 00:13:14.028
So,I'm sure you got a view of angela
that none of the family got to see.

00:13:14.028 --> 00:13:16.101
Tell me,what was she like?

00:13:16.101 --> 00:13:17.704
What was she really like?

00:13:17.704 --> 00:13:19.697
She was great...

00:13:19.697 --> 00:13:23.163
Just...great.

00:13:23.163 --> 00:13:25.747
I mean,she was so...

00:13:28.281 --> 00:13:29.503
Great.

00:13:29.503 --> 00:13:31.957
Yeah.

00:13:32.458 --> 00:13:34.802
Yeah.

00:13:38.197 --> 00:13:41.122
You two must have been really close,huh?

00:13:42.374 --> 00:13:44.608
We were.

00:13:45.129 --> 00:13:47.172
But it's not just her, it's matt.

00:13:47.653 --> 00:13:49.155
Who?

00:13:49.155 --> 00:13:50.758
Angela's boyfriend.

00:13:50.758 --> 00:13:52.861
Right -Matt.

00:13:53.252 --> 00:13:54.714
Uh,what about him?

00:13:54.714 --> 00:13:57.249
He killed himself last night.

00:13:57.249 --> 00:14:00.514
He cut his own throat. Who does that?

00:14:01.285 --> 00:14:03.809
That'S...terrible.

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:07.976
He was taking angela's death
pretty hard,and I guess...

00:14:09.939 --> 00:14:12.874
I mean,he'd been messed
up about it for days.

00:14:12.874 --> 00:14:14.116
Messed up how?

00:14:14.116 --> 00:14:17.011
He kept saying that
he saw her everywhere.

00:14:17.011 --> 00:14:18.934
Well,I'm -- I'm
sure that's normal.

00:14:18.934 --> 00:14:20.897
I mean,with everything
he was going through.

00:14:20.897 --> 00:14:23.612
He said that he saw her...

00:14:23.612 --> 00:14:26.777
As in an acid trip or something.

00:14:28.059 --> 00:14:30.243
Were angela and matt a happy couple?

00:14:30.243 --> 00:14:33.007
I mean,was there any reason that
angela would be angry with him?

00:14:33.007 --> 00:14:34.790
What?

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:37.554
No,of course not. Why do you ask?

00:14:37.925 --> 00:14:40.640
Just asking.

00:14:41.771 --> 00:14:44.366
Where did matt live?

00:14:44.366 --> 00:14:46.299
Next on cinemax,

00:14:46.299 --> 00:14:48.402
"Casa erotica iv,"

00:14:48.402 --> 00:14:51.427
A tale of two latin beauties,

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.612
Hey.

00:14:57.327 --> 00:14:58.990
What?

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:00.873
Awkward.

00:15:00.873 --> 00:15:03.667
Where the hell were you? Just
working my imaginary case.

00:15:04.879 --> 00:15:06.772
Yeah? And?

00:15:06.772 --> 00:15:09.567
Oh,well,you were right.
I didn't find much.

00:15:09.567 --> 00:15:12.502
Yeah. Except angela's
boyfriend died last night --

00:15:12.502 --> 00:15:15.116
Slit his own throat,
but,you know,that's normal.

00:15:15.557 --> 00:15:16.458
Uh,let's see. What else?

00:15:16.458 --> 00:15:20.294
Oh,he was seeing angela
everywhere before he died.

00:15:20.294 --> 00:15:23.630
But,you know,I'm sure  that's just
me transferring my own feelings.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.182
Okay,I get it.

00:15:25.182 --> 00:15:27.015
I'm sorry. Maybe there is
something going on here.

00:15:27.015 --> 00:15:28.668
Maybe?

00:15:28.668 --> 00:15:32.675
Sam,I know how to do my job
despite what you might think.

00:15:34.217 --> 00:15:36.561
We should check out the guy's apartment.

00:15:36.982 --> 00:15:39.125
I just came from there...

00:15:39.125 --> 00:15:42.060
A pile of dead plants
just like the cemetery.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.823
Hell,a dead goldfish,too.

00:15:43.823 --> 00:15:46.517
So,unholy ground? Maybe.

00:15:46.858 --> 00:15:50.504
I'm still not getting that powerful
angry-Spirit vibe from angela.

00:15:51.085 --> 00:15:53.078
I've been reading this, though.

00:15:58.357 --> 00:16:01.361
You stole the girl's diary? Yeah,sam.

00:16:02.734 --> 00:16:04.717
And if anything, the
girl's a little too nice.

00:16:04.717 --> 00:16:06.139
So,what do you want to do?

00:16:06.139 --> 00:16:07.932
Keep digging, talk to
more of her friends.

00:16:07.932 --> 00:16:10.466
You get any names? You kidding me?

00:16:10.917 --> 00:16:13.852
I have her bestest friend
in the whole wide world.

00:16:15.845 --> 00:16:18.459
I didn't realize the college
employed grief counselors.

00:16:18.459 --> 00:16:19.651
Oh,yeah.

00:16:19.651 --> 00:16:21.364
Yeah,you talk,we listen

00:16:21.364 --> 00:16:25.481
And maybe throw in a little therapeutic
collage whatever helps jump-Start the healing.

00:16:25.481 --> 00:16:28.766
Well,I think I'm okay. Thanks.

00:16:28.766 --> 00:16:31.711
Well,you heard what happened
to matt harrison,right?

00:16:31.711 --> 00:16:33.093
Yeah,I did.

00:16:33.093 --> 00:16:35.848
We just wanted to make
sure you were okay.

00:16:35.848 --> 00:16:39.253
Grief can make people do crazy things.

00:16:40.906 --> 00:16:44.602
Look,I'm sorry about
what happened to him.I am.

00:16:44.602 --> 00:16:47.577
But if matt killed himself,
it wasn't 'cause of grief.

00:16:47.577 --> 00:16:49.280
No? Then why?

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:51.313
It was guilt.

00:16:51.313 --> 00:16:53.667
Angie's death was matt's
fault, and he knew it.

00:16:53.667 --> 00:16:55.520
How was matt responsible?

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:57.944
She really loved that guy,

00:16:57.944 --> 00:17:01.530
But the night of the accident, she
walked in on him with another girl.

00:17:03.513 --> 00:17:06.818
She was really torn up.
That's why she crashed.

00:17:08.802 --> 00:17:10.294
Um,look, I got to get ready for work,

00:17:10.294 --> 00:17:15.723
So thanks for the concern,
but,seriously,I'll be okay.

00:17:21.142 --> 00:17:23.626
Well,my vengeful-Spirit theory is
starting to make a little more sense.

00:17:23.626 --> 00:17:26.230
I mean,hell hath no fury.

00:17:26.581 --> 00:17:30.307
So,if angela got her revenge
on matt,you think it's over?

00:17:31.649 --> 00:17:33.752
Well, there's one way to be sure.

00:17:35.485 --> 00:17:37.709
Yeah? What's that?

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:39.722
Burn the bones.

00:17:39.722 --> 00:17:41.786
Burn the bones?

00:17:42.236 --> 00:17:45.872
Are you high? Angela died last week.

00:17:45.872 --> 00:17:47.234
So?

00:17:47.234 --> 00:17:51.832
So there's not gonna be bones. There's
gonna be a ripe,rotting body in the coffin.

00:17:51.832 --> 00:17:54.807
Since when are you
afraid to get dirty,huh?

00:18:20.679 --> 00:18:22.532
Ladies first.

00:18:25.567 --> 00:18:27.490
Hold that.

00:19:03.219 --> 00:19:05.783
I missed you.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:30.303
They buried the body four days ago.

00:19:30.303 --> 00:19:32.777
I don't get it.

00:19:32.777 --> 00:19:34.370
Look.

00:19:38.096 --> 00:19:40.259
What is that? I'm not sure.

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:43.334
I've seen these kinds of symbols before.

00:19:45.808 --> 00:19:49.224
Dean,take it easy,okay?

00:19:56.376 --> 00:19:58.018
You're angie's friends.

00:19:58.018 --> 00:20:00.552
Dr. Mason --
We need to talk.

00:20:01.364 --> 00:20:03.097
Well,come in.

00:20:04.078 --> 00:20:05.581
Thanks.

00:20:08.706 --> 00:20:10.839
You teach ancient greek.

00:20:10.839 --> 00:20:12.862
Tell me...

00:20:13.243 --> 00:20:15.327
What are these?

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.862
I don't understand.

00:20:18.862 --> 00:20:21.607
You said this had
something to do with angela.

00:20:21.607 --> 00:20:24.742
It does. Please,just humor me.

00:20:26.705 --> 00:20:29.720
They're part of an ancient
greek divination ritual.

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:32.244
Used for necromancy,right. That's right.

00:20:32.244 --> 00:20:33.366
See, before we came over here,

00:20:33.366 --> 00:20:36.551
We stopped by the library and
did a little homework ourselves.

00:20:36.551 --> 00:20:40.698
Apparently, they use rituals like this
one for communicating with the dead,

00:20:40.698 --> 00:20:44.594
Even bringing corpses back to
life -Full-On zombie action.

00:20:44.594 --> 00:20:46.507
Yeah.

00:20:46.507 --> 00:20:49.773
I mean, according to the legends.

00:20:51.085 --> 00:20:52.738
Now,what's this all about?

00:20:52.738 --> 00:20:54.801
I think you know. Dean.

00:20:55.242 --> 00:20:56.834
Look,I get it.

00:20:56.834 --> 00:21:00.040
There are people that I would
give anything to see again,

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.212
But what gives you the right?

00:21:01.212 --> 00:21:02.464
Dean. What are you talking about?

00:21:02.464 --> 00:21:04.026
What's dead should stay dead! What?

00:21:04.026 --> 00:21:06.490
Stop it! What you brought
back isn't your daughter!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.014
These things are
vicious, they're violent!

00:21:09.014 --> 00:21:11.168
They're so nasty, they
rot the ground around them.

00:21:11.168 --> 00:21:13.862
I mean,come on! Haven't
you seen "pet sematary"?

00:21:13.862 --> 00:21:16.476
You're insane.

00:21:16.877 --> 00:21:19.712
Where is she? Get out of my house.

00:21:19.712 --> 00:21:21.985
I know you're hiding her
somewhere. Where is she?!

00:21:21.985 --> 00:21:24.299
Dean,stop! That's
enough. Dean,look --

00:21:24.299 --> 00:21:28.526
Beautiful,living plants. We're leaving.

00:21:28.526 --> 00:21:30.700
I'm calling the police. Sir,we're sorry.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:33.364
We won't bother you again.

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:38.402
What the hell's the
matter with you? Back off.

00:21:38.402 --> 00:21:40.746
That man is innocent.
He didn't deserve that.

00:21:40.746 --> 00:21:43.010
So she's not here. Maybe he's
keeping her somewhere else.

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:45.173
Stop it! That's enough,okay? Enough!

00:21:45.173 --> 00:21:47.527
Sam,I know what I'm doing.
No,you don'T...at all.

00:21:48.799 --> 00:21:51.053
I don't scare easy,but you're
scaring the crap out of me.

00:21:51.053 --> 00:21:52.525
Don't be overdramatic, sam.

00:21:52.525 --> 00:21:54.479
You're lucky this turned
out to be a real case,

00:21:54.479 --> 00:21:57.574
'Cause if it wasn't,you would've
found something else to kill.

00:21:57.574 --> 00:21:59.467
You're on edge, you're erratic,

00:21:59.467 --> 00:22:02.281
Except for when you're hunting,'cause
then you're downright scary.

00:22:02.281 --> 00:22:04.275
You're tailspinning,man,

00:22:04.275 --> 00:22:07.790
And you refuse to talk about it,
and you won't let me help you.

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:09.283
I can take care of myself, thanks.

00:22:09.283 --> 00:22:11.166
No,you can't!

00:22:11.166 --> 00:22:14.441
And you're the only one who
thinks you should have to.

00:22:14.441 --> 00:22:16.845
You don't have to handle
this on your own. No one can.

00:22:16.845 --> 00:22:20.601
If you bring up dad's death one more
time -- Dean,it's killing you. Please.

00:22:23.115 --> 00:22:25.800
We've already lost dad.

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:27.643
We lost mom.

00:22:27.643 --> 00:22:30.678
I've lost jessica.

00:22:30.678 --> 00:22:33.643
And now I'm gonna lose you,too?

00:22:35.365 --> 00:22:38.040
We better get out of
here before the cops come.

00:22:39.462 --> 00:22:41.656
I hear you,okay?

00:22:41.656 --> 00:22:44.390
I'm being an ass, and I'm sorry.

00:22:44.390 --> 00:22:48.136
But we got a freakin' zombie running
around. We need to figure out how to kill it.

00:22:51.131 --> 00:22:52.884
Right?

00:22:52.884 --> 00:22:55.308
Our lives are weird,man.

00:22:55.308 --> 00:22:57.592
You're telling me.

00:22:58.543 --> 00:23:01.148
Come on.

00:23:02.249 --> 00:23:05.224
Honey, is something bothering you?

00:23:06.797 --> 00:23:08.650
It's about matt.

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:10.503
Haven't we already talked about that?

00:23:10.503 --> 00:23:11.705
I
know,but,uh --

00:23:11.705 --> 00:23:15.271
Haven't we wasted enough
time on him already?

00:23:16.012 --> 00:23:18.987
Come sit down.

00:23:25.988 --> 00:23:29.544
You always said that
he didn't deserve me.

00:23:30.155 --> 00:23:32.799
You were right. Angela...

00:23:35.233 --> 00:23:38.989
You didn't get out and go see matt or...

00:23:38.989 --> 00:23:41.173
I've been here the whole time.

00:23:42.886 --> 00:23:47.443
Neal...you really think I
could do something like that?

00:23:47.443 --> 00:23:50.158
No,I... I don't know.

00:23:50.899 --> 00:23:53.713
I can't help it. You just -You seem...

00:23:53.713 --> 00:23:55.586
Different?

00:23:56.488 --> 00:23:59.583
You're right. I am.

00:24:02.247 --> 00:24:04.982
I've realized...

00:24:04.982 --> 00:24:08.548
You're the only one who
ever really loved me.

00:24:10.531 --> 00:24:15.028
You proved that. You brought me back.

00:24:15.028 --> 00:24:17.532
I'm with you now.

00:24:18.374 --> 00:24:21.679
Isn't that what you always wanted?

00:24:24.714 --> 00:24:26.978
We can't just waste
her with a head shot?

00:24:26.978 --> 00:24:29.802
Dude,you've been wahing
way too many romero flicks.

00:24:29.802 --> 00:24:31.906
You're telling me there's
no lore on how to smoke them?

00:24:31.906 --> 00:24:34.230
No,I'm telling you there's too much.

00:24:34.230 --> 00:24:36.313
There's 100 different
legends on the walking dead,

00:24:36.313 --> 00:24:38.216
But they all have different
methods for killing them.

00:24:38.216 --> 00:24:42.643
Some say setting them on
fire. One said -Where is it?

00:24:42.643 --> 00:24:45.007
Right here -Feeding
their hearts to wild dogs.

00:24:45.007 --> 00:24:46.840
That's my personal favorite.

00:24:46.840 --> 00:24:48.503
But who knows what's
real and what's myth?

00:24:48.503 --> 00:24:50.086
Is there anything they have in common?

00:24:50.086 --> 00:24:52.319
No,but a few said silver might work.

00:24:52.319 --> 00:24:53.812
Silver's a start.

00:24:53.812 --> 00:24:55.544
But now how are we going to find angela?

00:24:55.544 --> 00:24:57.227
We got to figure out
who brought her back.

00:24:57.227 --> 00:24:58.850
Any ideas?

00:24:58.850 --> 00:25:01.905
I think if it's not her dad,
it might be that guy,neal.

00:25:01.905 --> 00:25:03.307
Neal? Yep.

00:25:03.307 --> 00:25:06.082
How'd you come up with that?
Well,you got your journal,I got mine.

00:25:07.384 --> 00:25:08.896
"Neal's a real shoulder to cry on.

00:25:08.896 --> 00:25:12.693
He so understands what I'm
going through with matt."

00:25:12.693 --> 00:25:16.789
There's more here where that came from. It's
got unrequited duckie love written all over it.

00:25:16.789 --> 00:25:19.273
But that doesn't mean he
brought her back from the dead.

00:25:19.273 --> 00:25:21.807
Hmm,did I mention that
he's professor mason's T.A.?

00:25:21.807 --> 00:25:24.742
Has access to all the same books.

00:25:30.191 --> 00:25:31.994
Hello?

00:25:35.480 --> 00:25:37.503
Neal!

00:25:38.144 --> 00:25:40.909
It's your grief counselors.
We've come to hug.

00:25:44.484 --> 00:25:45.947
Silver bullets?

00:25:45.947 --> 00:25:49.152
Yeah,enough to make her
rattle like a change purse.

00:26:15.445 --> 00:26:17.849
Unless it's where he keeps his porn.

00:26:45.765 --> 00:26:48.309
It sure looks like a zombie pen to me.

00:26:48.309 --> 00:26:49.721
Yeah.

00:26:50.192 --> 00:26:52.265
An empty one.

00:26:53.708 --> 00:26:56.632
You think angela's gone after somebody?

00:27:06.078 --> 00:27:08.141
No,I think she went
out to rent "beaches."

00:27:08.141 --> 00:27:11.216
Look,smartass. She might kill someone.

00:27:11.216 --> 00:27:13.460
We got to find her,dean.

00:27:13.911 --> 00:27:16.084
Yeah.

00:27:16.645 --> 00:27:19.630
All right,she clipped matt
because he was cheating,right?

00:27:19.630 --> 00:27:20.632
Yeah.

00:27:20.632 --> 00:27:25.409
Well,takes two to,you
know, have hard-Core sex.

00:27:26.291 --> 00:27:27.353
I don't know. It just seemed

00:27:27.353 --> 00:27:29.887
That angela's roommate was...

00:27:29.887 --> 00:27:33.032
Broken up over matt's death.

00:27:33.473 --> 00:27:37.800
I mean, like really broken up.

00:27:55.809 --> 00:27:57.983
Hello?

00:28:05.725 --> 00:28:07.819
Hi,lindsay. I'm home.

00:28:17.024 --> 00:28:19.017
You know what you did.

00:28:21.842 --> 00:28:22.994
I'm sorry!

00:28:22.994 --> 00:28:24.586
I am so sorry!

00:28:24.586 --> 00:28:26.409
Not sorry enough!

00:28:49.016 --> 00:28:50.188
God.

00:28:51.871 --> 00:28:53.563
God.

00:28:53.563 --> 00:28:55.036
Oh,my god.

00:28:55.036 --> 00:28:56.298
Oh,my god.

00:29:26.808 --> 00:29:28.350
I got you. I got you.

00:29:31.526 --> 00:29:33.599
Damn, that dead chick can run.

00:29:33.599 --> 00:29:35.843
What now?

00:29:36.343 --> 00:29:38.767
I say we go have a
little chat with neal.

00:29:42.473 --> 00:29:45.488
So,the silver bullets,
they did something,right?

00:29:45.488 --> 00:29:48.974
Yeah,something,but not
enough. What else you got?

00:29:50.076 --> 00:29:51.548
Um,okay,besides silver,

00:29:51.548 --> 00:29:55.024
We have "nailing the undead
back into their grave beds."

00:29:55.024 --> 00:29:59.391
It's mentioned a few times. It's probably
where the whole vampire-Staking lore came from.

00:29:59.391 --> 00:30:01.595
Their grave beds? You serious?

00:30:01.595 --> 00:30:02.626
Yeah.

00:30:02.626 --> 00:30:05.842
How the hell are we gonna get
angela back to the cemetery?

00:30:17.350 --> 00:30:19.334
What are you guys doing here?

00:30:20.966 --> 00:30:24.111
You know,I've heard of some people doing
some pretty desperate things to get laid,

00:30:24.111 --> 00:30:25.834
But you

00:30:25.834 --> 00:30:28.018
You take the cake.

00:30:28.018 --> 00:30:29.610
Okay,who are you guys?

00:30:29.610 --> 00:30:31.964
You might want to ask
angela that question.

00:30:31.964 --> 00:30:34.108
What? We know what you did.

00:30:35.220 --> 00:30:38.225
The ritual...everything.

00:30:39.667 --> 00:30:41.089
You're crazy.

00:30:41.089 --> 00:30:44.425
Your girlfriend's past her
expiration date, and we're crazy?

00:30:44.815 --> 00:30:47.560
When someone's gone,
they should stay gone.

00:30:47.560 --> 00:30:50.475
You don't mess with that kind of stuff.

00:30:50.475 --> 00:30:52.728
Angela killed matt.

00:30:52.728 --> 00:30:55.673
She tried to kill lindsay.

00:30:55.673 --> 00:30:58.958
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:31:01.092 --> 00:31:03.025
Hey,no more crap,neal!

00:31:03.025 --> 00:31:05.499
This blood is on your hands.

00:31:05.499 --> 00:31:09.355
Now,me and him can make this right,
but you got to tell us where she is.

00:31:10.247 --> 00:31:12.030
Tell us!

00:31:14.183 --> 00:31:16.157
My house.

00:31:16.157 --> 00:31:18.160
She's at my house.

00:31:28.326 --> 00:31:30.660
You sure about that?

00:31:40.356 --> 00:31:42.610
Listen. It doesn't really
matter where she is.

00:31:43.812 --> 00:31:46.346
There's only one way to stop her.

00:31:46.346 --> 00:31:50.903
We've got to perform another ritual over
her grave  to reverse the one that you did.

00:31:51.614 --> 00:31:54.860
We're going to need some black
roots, some scar weed,some candles.

00:31:54.860 --> 00:31:56.863
It's very complicated, but
it will get the job done.

00:31:56.863 --> 00:31:59.357
She'll be dead again in a couple hours.

00:31:59.357 --> 00:32:01.591
I think you should come with us.

00:32:04.986 --> 00:32:08.662
I'm serious,neal.
Leave with us right now.

00:32:08.662 --> 00:32:10.355
No.

00:32:11.116 --> 00:32:13.039
No.

00:32:17.757 --> 00:32:19.961
Listen to me.

00:32:19.961 --> 00:32:22.315
Get out of here as soon as you can.

00:32:23.376 --> 00:32:27.313
But most of all,be cool.
No sudden movements.

00:32:27.313 --> 00:32:30.288
Don't make her mad.

00:32:33.192 --> 00:32:34.705
Let's go.

00:32:51.402 --> 00:32:53.205
You said you'd stay in the house.

00:32:53.205 --> 00:32:56.571
I'm sorry. I just needed to see you.

00:32:56.851 --> 00:32:59.345
Neal,please.

00:33:01.479 --> 00:33:04.403
You have to help me.

00:33:07.108 --> 00:33:08.731
Oh,god.

00:33:08.731 --> 00:33:12.126
Come with me to the cemetery.
Neal,they're trying to kill me.

00:33:12.126 --> 00:33:13.659
We have to stop them.

00:33:13.659 --> 00:33:15.822
You mean kill them?

00:33:17.124 --> 00:33:19.117
It's
true --

00:33:19.117 --> 00:33:22.142
Matt and lindsay. They hurt me.

00:33:22.834 --> 00:33:25.939
If you love me,you'll make
sure nobody hurts me again.

00:33:25.939 --> 00:33:29.354
Take me to the cemetery,
then all this will be over.

00:33:29.354 --> 00:33:32.529
We can start new lives together.

00:33:34.623 --> 00:33:36.606
Okay.

00:33:37.868 --> 00:33:40.512
God help me,but okay.

00:33:41.304 --> 00:33:43.648
I'll go get the car.

00:33:43.648 --> 00:33:45.080
Just...

00:33:45.080 --> 00:33:47.253
Just wait here.

00:34:10.582 --> 00:34:12.575
Neal,you look nervous.

00:34:13.146 --> 00:34:15.249
No,I'm fine.

00:34:16.541 --> 00:34:19.556
Were you... going to leave me?

00:34:19.987 --> 00:34:21.550
No,of course not.

00:34:21.550 --> 00:34:23.893
You were,weren't you?!

00:34:23.893 --> 00:34:27.269
How could you?! Neal,I loved you!

00:34:27.269 --> 00:34:28.501
Angela
--

00:34:41.262 --> 00:34:43.836
You really think this is gonna work?

00:34:43.836 --> 00:34:46.420
No,not really.

00:34:48.443 --> 00:34:51.248
But it was the only thing
I could come up with.

00:35:46.599 --> 00:35:49.593
Wait. It's not what you think.

00:35:49.593 --> 00:35:52.869
I didn't ask to be brought
back, but it's still me.

00:35:52.869 --> 00:35:55.904
I'm still a person. Please.

00:36:31.913 --> 00:36:33.966
Please don't!

00:36:50.783 --> 00:36:53.328
What's dead should stay dead.

00:37:01.681 --> 00:37:03.053
Rest in peace.

00:37:03.053 --> 00:37:05.217
Yeah, for good this time,okay?

00:37:11.678 --> 00:37:13.350
You know,

00:37:13.761 --> 00:37:15.524
The whole fake-Ritual thing,

00:37:15.524 --> 00:37:19.400
Luring angela into the
cemetery -Pretty sharp.

00:37:19.400 --> 00:37:21.333
Thanks.

00:37:21.333 --> 00:37:23.918
But did we have to use me as bait?

00:37:23.918 --> 00:37:27.784
I figured you were more her type,you
know? She had pretty crappy taste in guys.

00:37:28.195 --> 00:37:30.368
I think she broke my hand.

00:37:30.869 --> 00:37:34.194
You're just too fragile.
We'll get it looked at later.

00:37:39.593 --> 00:37:41.807
You want to stay for a while?

00:37:46.525 --> 00:37:48.618
No.

00:38:56.158 --> 00:38:58.222
Dean,what is it?

00:39:02.278 --> 00:39:03.751
I'm sorry.

00:39:05.273 --> 00:39:07.236
For what?

00:39:08.969 --> 00:39:11.604
The way I've been acting.

00:39:29.463 --> 00:39:31.706
And for dad.

00:39:34.150 --> 00:39:37.306
Well, he was your dad,too.

00:39:38.097 --> 00:39:39.900
It's my fault that he's gone.

00:39:39.900 --> 00:39:41.783
What are you talking about?

00:39:41.783 --> 00:39:44.738
I know you've been
thinking it. So have I.

00:39:45.559 --> 00:39:48.103
Doesn't take a genius to figure it out.

00:39:49.485 --> 00:39:53.782
Back at the hospital,
I had a full recovery.

00:39:53.782 --> 00:39:56.567
It was a miracle.

00:39:56.567 --> 00:39:59.332
And five minutes later, dad's
dead,and the colt's gone.

00:39:59.332 --> 00:40:02.988
You can't tell me there's
not a connection there.

00:40:04.821 --> 00:40:07.866
I don't know how the demon was involved.

00:40:08.356 --> 00:40:11.862
I don't know how the whole
thing went down exactly...

00:40:12.413 --> 00:40:15.979
But dad's dead because of me.

00:40:15.979 --> 00:40:17.601
And that much I do know.

00:40:17.601 --> 00:40:20.005
We don't know that, not for sure.

00:40:20.005 --> 00:40:23.000
Sam...

00:40:24.262 --> 00:40:28.289
You and dad...

00:40:29.531 --> 00:40:32.516
You're the most important
people in my life.

00:40:32.947 --> 00:40:36.592
And now...

00:40:36.993 --> 00:40:40.569
I never should have come
back, sam. It wasn't natural.

00:40:42.061 --> 00:40:44.916
And now look what's come of it.

00:40:47.230 --> 00:40:49.494
I was dead.

00:40:50.635 --> 00:40:54.121
And I should have stayed dead.

00:40:59.750 --> 00:41:02.835
You wanted to know how I was feeling.

00:41:04.328 --> 00:41:07.102
Well,that's it.

00:41:09.576 --> 00:41:11.610
So tell me.

00:41:16.317 --> 00:41:19.913
What could you possibly
say to make that all right?

00:00:01.743 --> 00:00:03.246
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
